# Region_Connections.mmd

## Purpose
A single region's connection diagram. What it holds depends on the region's rating: for SAFE
and WILD it is the typed graph of the region's locations; for DANGEROUS it is a
block-to-block graph asserting existence only, with the typed location graphs living one per
block.

## Context
Read first:
- `GENRE.md`
- `BRIEF.md` - this build's design requests, which replace this template's defaults where they speak
- this region's `Locations.md`
- this region's Overview, `setting/region/[Code].md`

## Instructions

**SAFE and WILD - the typed location graph.** These regions carry no blocks, so this diagram
is the location tier and carries type. It may be directional and should indicate connection
types where they matter to how a party moves through the region. Its shape, by default:

```
SAFE - a shallow hub
  1     Every location reachable from the settlement itself, independently
  1     No location gated behind another
  20%   One location outside the walls or past the edge of settlement

WILD - a forest of trees
  1     Every landmark reachable from the region's entry, independently of the others;
        landmarks do not interconnect
  1     At least two landmarks carrying children
  1     Hidden children connect to their parent with a normal edge
  1     Secret children connect to their parent with a hidden (-.-) edge
  1     Depth stops at three - a secret carries no children of its own
  20%   A landmark connecting onward to a neighbouring region
```

Which parents carry children decides how much of a WILD region sits behind something: a
parent states a lead for each child the graph gives it, so a child whose parent states
nothing is unreachable.

Connection type reference:
- `A --- B` normal - an open, two-way passage or path
- `A -.- B` hidden - a concealed, sealed, or secret connection
- `A --> B` one-way - only traversable in the direction shown

**DANGEROUS - the block-existence graph.** A DANGEROUS region is generated block by block,
so this diagram is a group tier: it states which blocks connect to which and nothing else -
no type, no direction, no quantity, per `templates/Connections.mmd`'s rule one tier up. The
typed edges between the locations of two connected blocks are written in the block diagrams
themselves, per `templates/Block_Connections.mmd`.

**Locations connect only to locations.** A location never connects to a block or a region,
so a block node and a location node never appear in the same diagram.

## Template

SAFE and WILD:
```mermaid
graph LR
    A1["[Code] [Location Name]"] --- A2["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A2 -.- A3["[Code] [Location Name]"]
    A3 --> A4["[Code] [Location Name]"]
```

DANGEROUS:
```mermaid
graph LR
    B1["[Block Name]"] --- B2["[Block Name]"]
    B2 --- B3["[Block Name]"]
```
